      whyItWorks:
        "A constitution is a set of rules, and rules only work if the people running them want them to. Weimar's weaknesses — unstable coalitions and an emergency power that could bypass parliament — mattered little while times were good. When crisis came, PR made a stable majority impossible and Article 48 gave an easy way round democracy, so power slid towards the President and the elites who chose the Chancellor.",
