      whyItWorks:
        "Money only works because people trust it. When the government printed money to pay the Ruhr strikers, trust collapsed and prices spiralled. The damage outlasted the crisis: millions of middle-class Germans lost their savings and blamed the republic, and they would be ready to listen to extremists when the next crisis came in 1929.",
      strategies: ["Link the factors", "Ask “who benefits?”", "Use precise evidence"],
